# Disable line-ending conversion for every file in this repo.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# `contentHash` in the published index is the sha256 of a skill's SKILL.md, and
# it is what pins the `curated` trust label to an exact byte sequence. If git
# rewrote CRLF to LF on checkout, the same file would hash differently on macOS
# and on the Linux CI runner, and every curated record would silently demote to
# `listed` the moment CI rebuilt the index.
#
# Turning conversion off makes a checkout byte-identical to what
# raw.githubusercontent.com serves. That is what lets the builder read a skill
# from disk when the record points at this very repo, instead of fetching a
# branch that does not yet contain the skill the pull request is adding.
* -text
